1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,533
The balloon comes out.

2
00:00:02,043 --> 00:00:04,087
What stays inside the artery?

3
00:00:04,528 --> 00:00:06,676
This is a drug-eluting stent.

4
00:00:07,117 --> 00:00:11,157
Its metal mesh supports the treated
section, and a medicine coating helps

5
00:00:11,238 --> 00:00:13,618
reduce the chance of narrowing again.

6
00:00:14,222 --> 00:00:17,311
A coronary stent is a tiny mesh tube.

7
00:00:17,752 --> 00:00:21,455
The mesh helps hold open a section of an
artery that was narrowed.

8
00:00:21,966 --> 00:00:26,738
In a drug-eluting stent, a coating
releases medicine near the treated area.

9
00:00:27,179 --> 00:00:29,513
The scaffold gives mechanical support.

10
00:00:29,722 --> 00:00:33,901
The medicine helps limit excess tissue
growth as the artery heals.

11
00:00:34,342 --> 00:00:37,918
The illustration shows a balloon-
expandable coronary stent.

12
00:00:38,359 --> 00:00:41,401
The stent is already mounted around a
folded balloon.

13
00:00:41,912 --> 00:00:45,279
The delivery catheter follows the wire
across the narrowing.

14
00:00:45,604 --> 00:00:47,554
The balloon expands the mesh.

15
00:00:47,879 --> 00:00:52,349
Then the team deflates and removes the
balloon and catheter, leaving the mesh in

16
00:00:52,419 --> 00:00:53,150
place.

17
00:00:53,661 --> 00:00:57,806
The medicine comes from the coating on the
stent and acts near the treated vessel

18
00:00:57,875 --> 00:01:03,077
wall. Over time it helps reduce the chance
that tissue growth will narrow that

19
00:01:03,146 --> 00:01:07,500
section again. Stent designs and coatings
differ.

20
00:01:07,825 --> 00:01:12,910
The expanded mesh continues to support the
treated section as the artery heals.

21
00:01:13,607 --> 00:01:17,264
A drug-coated balloon delivers medicine in
a different way.

22
00:01:17,775 --> 00:01:20,074
The medicine is on the balloon’s surface.

23
00:01:20,678 --> 00:01:25,345
While the balloon is inflated, some
medicine transfers to the treated tissue.

24
00:01:25,856 --> 00:01:27,586
The balloon then comes out.

25
00:01:28,096 --> 00:01:32,798
In a balloon-only treatment, that balloon
leaves no new metal scaffold.

26
00:01:33,402 --> 00:01:38,441
After placing a stent, the team checks the
treated area and the flow beyond it on

27
00:01:38,534 --> 00:01:43,759
contrast X-rays. In selected cases, a
small imaging device can

28
00:01:43,817 --> 00:01:46,998
help the team look at the stent from
inside the artery.

29
00:01:47,602 --> 00:01:52,071
These checks help the team assess whether
the mesh has opened as intended.

30
00:01:52,675 --> 00:01:57,052
The medicine released by the coating and
the antiplatelet medicines prescribed

31
00:01:57,110 --> 00:01:59,664
after the procedure have different jobs.

32
00:02:00,268 --> 00:02:03,286
The coating helps limit tissue growth near
the stent.

33
00:02:03,797 --> 00:02:07,257
Antiplatelet medicines help reduce the
chance of a clot.

34
00:02:07,954 --> 00:02:12,992
Your care team chooses your medicine plan
and explains how long it applies to you.

35
00:02:13,596 --> 00:02:16,696
A stent treats a specific section of an
artery.

36
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:20,864
Coronary artery disease still needs
ongoing care.

37
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:26,181
At follow-up, your team can explain what
was treated, how the medicine plan fits

38
00:02:26,216 --> 00:02:29,977
your situation, and what to do if symptoms
return.

39
00:02:30,790 --> 00:02:34,412
The next episode looks at how a drug-
coated balloon works.
